      {
        question: "How do I know if my garage door spring is broken?",
        answer: "<p>The most obvious sign is a loud bang—it sounds like a gunshot or firecracker. You might also notice your garage door won't open more than a few inches, the door feels extremely heavy when you try to lift it manually, or the opener motor runs but the door doesn't move. If you see a gap in the spring coil (it looks like it's split in two), your spring is definitely broken. Our free <a href=\"/homeowner-tools/door-diagnosis\">DoorDiagnosis™ tool</a> can help you confirm the issue in under 60 seconds.</p>"
      },
      {
        question: "Should I replace one spring or both?",
