<ServicePage {...content} schema={[springSchema]}>
  <ServiceSection heading={"Fast, Safe Spring Repair You Can Trust"} image="/photos/Broken-spring.webp" imageAlt="Broken garage door spring showing gap in coil">
    <p> A broken spring doesn't just mean an inconvenient repair—it means your 200+ pound garage door has no counterbalance. Operating the door in this condition is NOT safe. It risks severe injury and damages to your opener and door. </p>
    <p> Our spring replacements restore your door's safety and reliability. We replace both springs (even if only one broke), balance your door, and test the entire system before we leave. </p>
  </ServiceSection>

  <ServiceSection heading={"How to Know If Your Spring Is Broken"} tone="sand">
    <ul><li><strong>Loud bang from the garage</strong> — sounds like a gunshot or firecracker (this is the spring breaking)</li><li><strong>Garage door only lifts a few inches</strong> or won't open at all</li><li><strong>Visible gap in the spring</strong> coil above the door (it looks split in two)</li><li><strong>Door feels extremely heavy</strong> when you try to lift it manually</li><li><strong>Opener motor runs but door doesn't move</strong> (motor can't lift the weight)</li></ul>
    <p><strong>Not sure what's wrong?</strong> Use our free <a href="/homeowner-tools/door-diagnosis#troubleshooting">DoorDiagnosis™ tool</a> to walk through common issues step-by-step. It takes less than 60 seconds. </p>
  </ServiceSection>

  <ServiceSection heading={"Why You Should Act Quickly"}>
    <p> We know it's tempting to try to "make it work" until you have time to deal with it. But operating a garage door with a broken spring is dangerous: </p>
    <ul><li><strong>Injury risk:</strong> The door can fall suddenly, causing serious harm</li><li><strong>Opener damage:</strong> Your opener isn't designed to lift your garage door without spring assistance—forcing it burns out the motor</li><li><strong>Second spring failure:</strong> If one spring broke, the other is about to fail</li></ul>
    <p><strong>Bottom line:</strong> Don't use the door until the spring is replaced. It's not safe, and it'll cost you more in the long run. </p>
    <p><a href="/homeowner-tools/easy-estimate#estimate-form" class="btn btn--primary">Get Instant Price Estimate</a></p>
  </ServiceSection>

  <ServiceHighlights heading={"Restoring Your Door’s Performance"} items={[{"title":"Repairs Done Right the First Time","body":"<p> When a spring breaks, the other one is usually close behind. We install a properly matched set so your door runs smoothly and you’re not facing another failure weeks later. </p>"},{"title":"High-Quality Springs","body":"<p> We provide rugged, high-performance springs that deliver smooth, dependable operation for every residential door. </p>"},{"title":"Full System Check Included","body":"<p> Every spring replacement includes door balancing, safety testing, and complete inspection at no extra charge. </p>"},{"title":"Warranty on Parts and Labor","body":"<p> We stand behind our work. If there's an issue with the springs we install, we make it right—everytime. </p>"},{"title":"Same-Day Service","body":"<p> We know you need your garage. Most Mt. Pleasant area calls get same-day service when available. </p>"}]} tone="sand" />

  <ToolPromo image="/photos/springstatus-logo.webp" imageAlt="SpringStatus torsion spring lifespan estimator" heading={"Curious How Much Life Your Springs Have Left?"} text={"Our free SpringStatus™ Tool helps you estimate the remaining lifespan of your garage door springs based on a few quick questions. Find out if you're due for replacement soon—before you hear that loud bang."} href="/homeowner-tools/spring-status#springstatus" label="Check Your Springs Now" />
</ServicePage>
